     "type": "intro",
     "title": "Why Has Obesity Tripled in 40 Years?",
     "content": "Since 1980, global obesity rates have **nearly tripled**. In the United States, roughly **42% of adults** now meet the clinical definition of obesity. Type 2 diabetes — once called 'adult-onset' — is exploding among teenagers.\n\nHere's the strange part: we know more about nutrition than ever. Gyms are everywhere. Low-fat foods fill the shelves. We count calories on our watches.\n\nSo why is the epidemic accelerating?\n\nDr. **Jason Fung**, a Toronto nephrologist treating diabetic kidney disease, opens **The Obesity Code (2016)** with a startling claim: the standard advice — **'eat less, move more'** — has failed because it misunderstands what obesity actually is. Obesity, he argues, is not a **caloric** disorder. It is a **hormonal** disorder. And once you see that, everything changes.",
