     "explanation": "Fung's central critique is that CICO treats the body like an open system where you can cut intake without affecting output. In reality, when you eat less, the body **lowers metabolic rate** (BMR can drop 10-40%) and **raises hunger hormones** like ghrelin. Calories in and calories out are tightly **coupled** through hormonal feedback — that's why almost all caloric restriction diets fail long-term.",
