     "type": "example",
     "title": "Three Real Patient Stories",
     "content": "**Maria, 52, pre-diabetic, 35 lbs overweight**:\n• Started Level 1 protocol, eliminated sugary coffee creamer and afternoon snacks\n• Added 16:8 fasting at week 8\n• 6 months: down 28 lbs, HbA1c from 6.1 to 5.4, fasting insulin from 18 to 6\n• Felt 'human again' — energy back, fog gone\n• Now maintains at Level 2 indefinitely\n\n**David, 47, T2D on metformin + Lantus 30 units/day**:\n• Worked with endocrinologist while starting Fung protocol\n• Reduced Lantus by 2-4 units/week as glucose dropped\n• Off insulin by month 5; off metformin by month 11\n• HbA1c 8.2 → 5.5\n• Lost 52 lbs; cardiovascular risk profile transformed\n\n**Jennifer, 38, chronic stress, struggled with 'doing everything right'**:\n• Diet was already clean; weight stuck for 3 years\n• Real intervention: prioritized sleep (8 hr), cut afternoon coffee, added 2x/week strength\n• Lost only 12 lbs but **waist dropped 4 inches** (visceral fat)\n• Energy, mood, and metabolic markers improved dramatically\n• Lesson: sometimes it's not the diet — it's the cortisol\n\nThese aren't dramatic 100-lb stories. They're **realistic, sustainable outcomes** that played out over **6-12 months** with consistent protocol adherence. The pattern: identify the **dominant driver** (composition, timing, or stress), focus there first, then layer in the rest.",
